NAME
    vectors - print interrupt vector targets resolved through labels

SYNOPSIS
    vectors

DESCRIPTION
    Reads the attached core's live interrupt vector table through CpuBus
    and prints each vector's target address, annotated with any matching
    symbol from label(1). Because vectors are read live from the bus, bank
    switches and runtime vector remapping are reflected immediately.

    On processors with multiple vector modes (such as 65816 native and
    emulation modes), vectors are grouped by mode. When execution coverage
    is enabled (see cov(1)), vectors whose target address has executed are
    marked '(ran)'.

EXAMPLES
    vectors
    cov on; vectors

EXIT STATUS
    0   Vector table printed.
    1   No target attached or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    runto(1), bt(1), cov(1), label(1), addr(1), regs(1)
